Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S08
Scenario title: Meeting Room Reservation
Initial workflow description:
A meeting room is reserved for a team meeting. The organizer checks availability and shares the room information with participants.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer use to check room availability and submit the reservation request?",
      "answer": "Typically some kind of tool or platform is used, but the exact method can vary depending on what's available at the time."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Is any approval or confirmation required from a facilities team or administrator before the reservation is considered confirmed?",
      "answer": "It depends — sometimes someone may need to sign off, but it's not always the case in every situation."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What happens when the requested room or time slot is already booked — does the organizer manually search for alternatives, or does the system suggest them?",
      "answer": "Usually the responsible person looks around for something else that might work, one way or another."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How is the confirmed room information communicated to participants, and is that notification step currently manual or system-generated?",
      "answer": "People tend to be informed somehow after things are sorted out, though the exact method isn't always consistent."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How are cancellations or changes to an existing reservation initiated and communicated to both the system and the participants?",
      "answer": "Changes are generally handled by whoever set things up, and others are informed in some fashion afterward."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Are there any required actions after the meeting concludes, such as formally releasing the room or logging whether the room was actually used?",
      "answer": "That kind of follow-up isn't really specified — it may or may not happen depending on the situation."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
Return JSON with this shape:
{
  "workflow": {
